course: dictionary
lesson: 5848
title: Male and female
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Male is a word we use to describe the sex of an animal or plant. A male cannot give birth or lay eggs, and in animals the male makes sperm. «A male lion» tells you it is the lion that is not the mother.
explain: Male can also be a noun, meaning one male person, animal or plant. In forms and science tables you will see «male / female», so you can tick the box that fits.
explain: Look at the words around male to find its meaning. In «male animals» or «male part», the context tells you that male is about sex, not about size or strength. Always check: does your meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: Male means belonging to the sex that cannot give birth or lay eggs.
fact: In many animals, males and females look different. A male lion has a mane, and a male peacock has a colourful tail.
fact: «All clownfish hatch as males, and the biggest one in a group can turn into the female.»
fact: «The red kangaroo is the largest marsupial; males wrestle and kick each other with their strong back legs.»
fact: In plants, male parts called stamens make pollen. Male is also used for a part that fits into a hole, such as a male plug.
exercise: In «a male lion», what does male tell you? | A lion with a long tail | A young lion that is not yet grown up | *The sex that cannot give birth or lay eggs | A lion that is very old
exercise: «All clownfish hatch as males, and the biggest one in a group can turn into the female.» What does «hatch as males» mean? | They can swim very fast | They are the biggest fish in the group | *They are born male | They are born female
exercise: «Male emperor penguins huddle in thousands, each with an egg on his feet.» What does male tell us here? | The penguins can hop very fast | The penguins live in hot deserts | The penguins are all chicks | *The penguins are the sex that holds the egg
test: Which word is the opposite of male, as on a form? | happy | huge | *female | mid
test: In plants, which part makes pollen? | seeds | *stamens | roots | petals
exam: Which phrase uses male for a part that fits into a hole? | a male lion | *a male plug | male animals | a male and a female
